  "body": "Home\nAbout us\nIndustries\nManufacturing and industrial\nArchitecture and Buildings\nServices\nScanning\nScan to BIM\nAs-Built Drafting\n3D Modeling\nBuilding analysis\nBOMA As-Built Digital Plans\nMatterport 3D Virtual Tours\nDigital Twins\nBlog\nCase studies\nContact\nGet in touch\n(514) 606-9604\nEnglish\nen\nFrançais\nfr\nProject manager, digitization and building design\nTo make a long story short.\npointSpace is a fast-growing technology company operating in the industrial and construction sectors. We use cutting-edge tools to provide the most accessible and versatile solution for geospatial data analysis. Our mission is to help businesses optimize their operations and drive growth by offering a versatile digital twin that simplifies the management of space, machinery, and equipment.\nYou are\ncreative-proactive-efficient-sympathetic-polyvalent-autodidact and passionate\nabout new technologies?\nRequired profile\nBackground in architecture, consulting engineering or other relevant building experience\nProficiency in Revit and AutoCAD software\nKnowledge of the SCAN TO BIM concept (asset)\nKnowledge of SketchUp (asset)\nBilingual (French, English)\nThe role and responsibilities of the position.\nYou will be responsible for projects involving the modelling of existing buildings using point clouds:\nCustomer relations\nData acquisition at project sites\nCoordination of the design phase with our partners\nQuality assurance\nIdeation, R&D projects new technologies?\nWhy join pointSpace?\nFirstly, it's a full-time position with a\nhyperflexible\nschedule. hyperflexible in hybrid mode as needed.\nBut above all, it's definitely a unique human adventure! It's a great opportunity to help a young, ambitious company grow.\nYou dream of being part of change in the industry?\nWe need your expertise! Let's talk!\nSend your resume\nContact us !\nLouis Dallaire\nldallaire@pointspace.ca\n(514) 606-9604\nContact Us\nFirst name\nLast name\nEmail\nMessage\nThank you for contacting us.\nWe will get back to you as soon as possible.\nOops, there was an error sending your message.\nPlease try again later.\nShare by:",
